## Outcome and conditions

Derive the simple-slope conditional variance, state the precise BLUE comparison class, calculate a conventional slope standard error/t statistic and degrees of freedom, and discriminate which assumptions support each property.

Required components (all must be elicited and passed):

- C1: Weighted-variance derivation with vanishing cross terms and correct noise/regressor-variation effects.
- C2: BLUE class and first 4/5/6 distinctions stated precisely.
- C3: Correct df, noise/slope variance, se and null-centered t with conditional decision.
- C4: Significance/exogeneity distinction and F joint-restriction purpose.

